&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;sales-oriented Alliance &amp;amp; Channel Professional &lt;/strong&gt;with experience and expertise in cybersecurity to lead, expand, and manage Onapsis’ Global Systems Integrator (GSI) partner ecosystem across EMEA. The ideal candidate has a proven track record of building, driving, and scaling joint go-to-market strategies with top-tier GSIs and global consulting firms, specifically Accenture, Deloitte, PwC, &lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-subtree=&quot;aimfl,mfl&quot;&gt;Capgemini&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;, IBM.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will be responsible for shaping our EMEA GSI alliance as a major commercial growth engine - translating partner relationships into co-sell pipeline, deal velocity, and measurable revenue contribution across European markets. The &lt;strong&gt;Director, Alliances EMEA (GSI)&lt;/strong&gt; will work closely with Onapsis field sales teams, regional leadership, and partner practice leads to align partner-led activities to the company’s strategic goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing, your legacy:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and coordinate all commercial, executive, and business development aspects of Onapsis’ strategic GSI alliance partners across EMEA (Accenture, Deloitte, PwC, CAPGemini, IBM), facilitating joint planning and aligning resources internally and externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a portfolio of joint solution offerings and repeatable use cases with GSI partners, embedding Onapsis into partner-led SAP digital transformation practices (S/4HANA migrations, RISE with SAP) and driving GTM execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive and manage partner-sourced and partner-influenced co-sell pipelines with GSI partners and Onapsis field sales teams, tracked and managed through Salesforce CRM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable partner-led implementation and managed services delivery models (MSSP / QuickStart packages), maximizing GSI service revenue opportunities around Onapsis platform deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and execute joint marketing initiatives, executive roundtables, and ABM campaigns with GSI partner marketing teams across target EMEA regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contract negotiations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7+ years of experience in enterprise software sales, business development, or alliance management &lt;/strong&gt;at a cybersecurity or enterprise software company, with at least &lt;strong&gt;5+ years directly managing GSIs &lt;/strong&gt;(Accenture, Deloitte, PwC, CAPGemini, IBM) across EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep existing network and executive relationships within the cybersecurity and SAP practices of major GSIs across key EMEA markets (UK&amp;amp;I, DACH, France, Nordics).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of building joint GTM playbooks and driving partner-sourced and partner-influenced pipeline in co-sell models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise and acumen in forging initiatives, go-to-market and pipeline development plans with business partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in selling in an overlay role in conjunction with field sales teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the SAP ecosystem (S/4HANA migrations, RISE with SAP, SAP BTP) and partner-led services delivery frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Past relationships with top national and regional VARs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success in exceeding revenue targets with partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills (both verbal and written). Able to position technical solutions as business value to ‘owners’ of Security Services offering portfolio in partner organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Solution Selling/Consultative Selling methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivery of comprehensive business plans with a multi-year outlook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical competencies and ability to communicate and present at an executive level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-disciplined team player that can work in a fast-paced dynamic start-up environment remotely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S. or equivalent experience. Masters or MBA a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: Remote in Germany.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive Compensation &amp;amp; Perks: An attractive salary package and extensive lifestyle benefits, including JobRad, Focus Fridays, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ultimate Flexibility &amp;amp; Balance: 30 days of paid vacation, flexible working hours, and the ability to work remotely from other EU countries by arrangement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-First Support: Dedicated backing for parents, including subsidized childcare (up to primary school age) and 5 fully paid sick days per child.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous Growth &amp;amp; Development: A tailored onboarding experience with a dedicated buddy program, alongside comprehensive professional training and English language courses.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empowering Culture: High autonomy and creative freedom within a solution-oriented environment, featuring flat hierarchies, respectful communication, and an innovative workplace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Onapsis:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Onapsis protects the business applications that run the global economy. The Onapsis Platform delivers vulnerability management, change assurance, and continuous compliance for business applications from leading vendors such as SAP, Oracle, and others. The Onapsis Platform is powered by the Onapsis Research Labs, the team responsible for the discovery and mitigation of more than 1,000 zero-day vulnerabilities in business applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Onapsis is headquartered in Boston, MA, with offices in Heidelberg, Germany and Buenos Aires, Argentina, and proudly serves hundreds of the world’s leading brands, including close to 30% of the Forbes Global 100, six of the top 10 automotive companies, five of the top 10 chemical companies, four of the top 10 technology companies, and three of the top 10 oil and gas companies.&lt;/p&gt;
