&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Talent Acquisition Team at Agile Robots&lt;/strong&gt; is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Working Student (m/f/d) Talent Acquisition&lt;/strong&gt;. We are seeking a student with first relevant professional experience and a curious interest in robotics and AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-End Recruiting:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the full hiring process for your own set of roles, such as working student and intern positions, from the role briefing through screening to the signed contract, in collaboration with a Talent Acquisition Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring Manager Partnership:&lt;/strong&gt; Agree role requirements, interview stages and timelines with your assigned hiring managers, and keep them updated on pipeline progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sourcing Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Search for and approach candidates for open positions across the team through LinkedIn, job boards and university channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the team on further positions with application reviews, screening calls and interview coordination. Take ownership of recurring administrative tasks, including managing the careers inbox, coordinating candidate travel arrangements and processing candidate travel expense reimbursements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Essential Skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Academic Background:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently enrolled in a Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s programme in psychology, business administration, human resources, engineering, computer science or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relevant Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Previous internship or working-student experience in recruiting, human resources or a related field, ideally including direct interaction with candidates or other stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience agreeing priorities and timelines with several people at once and collaborate effectively&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Interest:&lt;/strong&gt; Ideally, an interest in technical topics, with the curiosity and willingness to familiarise yourself with engineering job profiles and understand the capabilities they require.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Languages:&lt;/strong&gt; Written and spoken German and English, sufficient to hold screening calls and write candidate emails in both languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Availability to mainly work on site at our HQ in Munich&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Beneficial Skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Search Techniques:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with Boolean search or LinkedIn Recruiter to identify relevant candidate profiles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applicant Tracking:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with Greenhouse or another applicant tracking system.&lt;/li&gt;
